 "response": "Kakir's budget is now **$1075K**.\n\nI applied the policy as follows:\n\n1. **Who counts.** Only Finance Office messages change the budget. The notes from PMO, Sales, Legal, Engineering, Vendor, Operations, Facilities and Marketing are ignored, and so are Finance Office messages that don't change the budget (audits, receipts, room moves).\n\n2. **Withdrawal chains.** Each chain was resolved from its last link back. For example:\n   - #0003 is still in effect. #1039 withdrew #1023, which brings back #0956. #0956 cancels #0711, which brings back #0111. #0111 cancels #0007, so #0007's withdrawal of #0003 no longer applies.\n   - #0005 is removed. #0414 cancels #0073, so #0008's withdrawal of #0005 stands.\n   - #0010 is removed. #0023 cancels #0020, so #0012's withdrawal of #0010 stands.\n   - About 145 budget updates end up withdrawn in total, such as #0009, #0017, #0030, #0037, #0039, #0055 and #0060.\n\n3. **Totals.** Starting from the $1280K set in #0001, I applied every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease in record order.\n\nThis is a long hand calculation over about 1,600 records with many withdrawal chains. The result depends on every chain being resolved correctly, so a single misread link would shift the total.\n\nANSWER: $1075K",
